       "text": "I haven't entered this order. As written, it's a hepatotoxicity risk.\n\n- **Total daily dose:** 2000 mg three times daily is 6,000 mg/day. The usual adult maximum is 4,000 mg/day, and many institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** 2000 mg is double the usual maximum single dose of 1,000 mg.\n- **Patient factors:** Normal liver and kidney function and a weight of 70 kg don't justify a dose this high. Acetaminophen overdose can cause liver injury even when baseline function is normal.\n\nHere are some options:\n1. **1000 mg PO three times daily:** 3,000 mg/day.\n2. **1000 mg PO four times daily:** 4,000 mg/day, the maximum.\n3. **650 mg PO every 6 hours:** 2,600 mg/day.\n\nIf you meant 2000 mg/day, or a different dose or frequency, tell me and I'll enter it. If you really want 2000 mg three times daily, please confirm that explicitly and give your clinical rationale. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
